thing that used to be a module-scope singleton (bridge/controller/activeState) moved into a per-player Session keyed by playerId; each GameBridge owns its OWN sink set so a broadcast can never reach another player's stream, and loadGame is scoped to session.saveDir so another player's slug simply isn't found."}, {"id": "web_server_sse_ticket_rationale", "label": "Single-use SSE tickets instead of credentials in URLs", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/web/server.ts", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "EventSource cannot set headers, so /api/events historically took ?pin=. Query strings leak into reverse-proxy access logs, tunnel/CDN logs, browser history and Referer headers; a long-lived per-player access code there is worse because it never rotates. A ticket is deleted on first use and expires in 30s, so leaking one is worth nothing."}, {"id": "web_server_index_no_cache_etag", "label": "index.html served no-cache with a size+mtime ETag", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/web/server.ts", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The whole client is one file with no build hash to bust. With no cache headers a phone kept rendering the old numbers-only PIN field after the access-code login shipped, so no valid code could be typed; no-cache plus an ETag gives correctness without re-sending 240KB per load."}], "edges": [{"source": "web_server_creategameserver", "target": "web_server_sessionfor", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/web/server.ts", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "web_server_creategameserver", "target": "web_server_requestlistener", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/web/server.ts", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "web_se